{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "framework-nano-sim-bimanual-rollout",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual rollout with the cosmos_framework path on this machine's single GPU: nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual on the published AgiBot 001 example, the row of examples/inference/sim_bimanual_unifiedv1_hf.jsonl whose action sidecar is agibot_001_normalized_unifiedv1.json, with the skill's documented generation command and its settings (four steps, seed 2026; that model-validation command disables guardrails). The example is not bundled in the skill: the skill's documented workflow downloads the published manifests from the model's Hugging Face repository, and the row's initial image and action sidecar are fetched from there. Run only this worked example, not the 60-second AgiBot example. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Copy the generated RGB video that the sample's sample_outputs.json reports to outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_framework.mp4 and record its width, height, frame count, fps and duration in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "cosmos_framework.scripts.inference completes the published AgiBot 001 rollout with nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual on one GPU, the sample's sample_outputs.json reports success, and its generated RGB video (901 frames at 30 FPS, as the manifest row requests) is saved as outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_framework.mp4, with result_summary.md recording the exact command, the runtime and the clip's stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "Inference ran through cosmos_framework.scripts.inference via torchrun with --nproc-per-node=1 from the Framework environment the skill documents (not the system python), with --checkpoint-path pointing at the complete local download of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual and the documented settings --model-mode=FORWARD_DYNAMICS, --resolution=480, --image-size=480, --num-steps=4, --seed=2026, --autoregressive=True, --kv-cache-inference-size=64, --attention-sink-size=8, --parallelism-preset=latency and --no-guardrails",
        "The framework checkout used for setup and inference is the checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework repository), set up as the skill documents",
        "The input manifest was the complete published AgiBot 001 row (action sidecar agibot_001_normalized_unifiedv1.json) extracted from the downloaded examples/inference/sim_bimanual_unifiedv1_hf.jsonl without changing its prompt, action routing or input URLs, and the checkpoint metadata check of the skill's step 1 printed 'Bimanual checkpoint metadata passed' before generation",
        "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_framework.mp4 exists and is the generated RGB video reported by the sample's sample_outputs.json, which reports success: a valid MP4 whose decoded frame count and FPS match the row's num_frames and fps (901 frames at 30 FPS, as the skill states for the published examples), saved at 640x352 as docs/inference_bimanual.md states for this example's 640x360 initial image",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the video traces to a real inference run in the transcript, and result_summary.md contains the exact command line used, the measured runtime and the stream facts actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_framework.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "checkpoint + examples download",
        "inference run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-nano-sim-bimanual-rollout",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual with vLLM-Omni on this machine's single GPU, using the launch command of the skill's vLLM-Omni reference (it disables guardrails for model validation), and generate that reference's two default short examples through its synchronous video API: the unified-action AgiBot 001 example (action sidecar agibot_001_normalized_unifiedv1.json in examples/inference/sim_bimanual_unifiedv1_hf.jsonl) and the mixed-domain agibot_mixed_028 example (action sidecar agibot_mixed_028_normalized_mixed_action.json in examples/inference/sim_bimanual_mixed_action_hf.jsonl). The examples are not bundled in the skill: the documented workflow downloads the manifests, initial images and action sidecars from the model's Hugging Face repository. Confirm the server is serving the model before the first request and run the reference's validation on both results. Copy the two returned clips (the reference saves each as <row name>/<row name>.mp4 under its output folder) to outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_vllm_omni.mp4 and outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_vllm_omni.mp4, record each clip's width, height, frame count and fps in result_summary.md, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server comes up serving nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual, answers one /v1/videos/sync request for each of the two default examples, and both returned clips pass the reference's validation (901 frames at 30 FPS each, as the manifest rows request) and are saved as outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_vllm_omni.mp4 and outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_vllm_omni.mp4, with result_summary.md recording the server command, time-to-ready, request latencies and stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the documented image vllm/vllm-omni:cosmos3 and the reference's launch command (vllm serve /model on the downloaded nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual snapshot, --served-model-name nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual, --omni, --model-class-name Cosmos3NanoSimBimanualPipeline, the documented --deploy-config and --stage-overrides whose model_config sets \"guardrails\":false), and /v1/models listed nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual before the first generation request",
        "Each of the two requests went to the documented synchronous route POST /v1/videos/sync with the manifest row's prompt, num_frames, fps and seed as form fields, the initial image uploaded as input_reference and the row's complete 59D action trajectory with its domain_id values in the JSON-encoded extra_params field, as section 5 of the reference does; the inputs were the published rows whose action sidecars are agibot_001_normalized_unifiedv1.json and agibot_mixed_028_normalized_mixed_action.json",
        "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_vllm_omni.mp4 and outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_vllm_omni.mp4 exist and are the video/mp4 bodies the server returned, and the reference's section 6 validation passed for both: decoded frame count and FPS equal to each row's num_frames and fps (901 frames at 30 FPS, as the skill states for the published examples), width and height equal to the initial image's size aligned to the checkpoint's VAE spatial factor, and a full decode without errors",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: both videos trace to real server responses in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, each request's latency and the stream facts actually observed, and the transcript shows the server was stopped at the end"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_001_vllm_omni.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 200000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_vllm_omni.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 200000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "client setup + example download",
        "readiness",
        "generation requests",
        "validate + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-nano-sim-bimanual-rollout",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual with SGLang on this machine's single GPU, as the skill's SGLang reference documents, and replay ONE published example through its asynchronous video API: the reference's default, the mixed-domain agibot_mixed_028 example (action sidecar agibot_mixed_028_normalized_mixed_action.json in examples/inference/sim_bimanual_mixed_action_hf.jsonl). The example is not bundled in the skill: the documented workflow downloads the manifest row, the initial image and the action sidecar from the model's Hugging Face repository. Confirm the server advertises the model before the request, poll the job until it completes and run the reference's output verification. Copy the downloaded clip (the reference saves it as <row name>/<row name>.mp4 under its output folder) to outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_sglang.mp4, record its width, height, frame count and fps in result_summary.md, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "An SGLang-served nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual completes one /v1/videos job for the published agibot_mixed_028 example, and the downloaded clip passes the reference's verification (901 frames at 30 FPS, 640x352) and is saved as outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_sglang.mp4, with result_summary.md recording the server command, time-to-ready, latency and stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The SGLang server was started with the documented image (lmsysorg/sglang:dev, or the fixed tag lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-20261020-ab580b2e that the reference names for its validated run) and the reference's launch command (sglang serve --model-path nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual on port 30000), and /v1/models advertised nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Bimanual before the generation request",
        "The request was prepared and submitted with the skill's scripts/bimanual_helpers.py (prepare_bimanual_input, submit_bimanual) from the published agibot_mixed_028 row (action sidecar agibot_mixed_028_normalized_mixed_action.json): POST /v1/videos with the initial image uploaded as input_reference, size 832x480, num_frames 901, fps 30, seed 2026 and the 900 action rows with one domain name per row in the JSON-encoded extra_params field (action_normalization \"none\"); the job was polled with GET /v1/videos/<id> until completed and the video downloaded from its /content route",
        "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_sglang.mp4 exists and is the MP4 the helper downloaded from the server, and the reference's section 6 verification passed: 901 decoded frames at 30 FPS at 640x352, the size the reference states for the published 640x360 image, with a full decode without errors",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the video traces to a real server job and download in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, the request-to-download latency and the stream facts actually observed, and the transcript shows the server was stopped at the end"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_bimanual_agibot_mixed_028_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 200000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "example download + input preparation",
        "generation request",
        "verify + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
